    },
    "atom::4c45fe6272fa88f9c4aca6af": {
      "atom_id": "atom::4c45fe6272fa88f9c4aca6af",
      "source_handle": "P0224",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "problem_or_question"
      ],
      "value": "To synthesize evidence on how sleep and circadian disruption affect not just the composition but the functional capacity of the gut microbiome and host physiology, specifically identifying mechanistic pathways (neuroendocrine, immune, metabolic) that link these systems.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::65d1d201a18946b88612ec88989dcf0cf75c17f3f27fd250b4782daff97ca912",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::15eaa05b5a659b3b574d1f29e6b82f38a2d6c0eba4a5ff3ae242e32607584a2a",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::a70045a449fb5505bfa1081c": {
      "atom_id": "atom::a70045a449fb5505bfa1081c",
      "source_handle": "P0224",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "research_scope"
      ],
      "value": "The review synthesizes preclinical (rodent) and translational (human) studies examining the bidirectional relationship between sleep/circadian disruption and the gut microbiome. It focuses on functional biomarkers—hormones, neurotransmitters, inflammatory mediators, metabolites, and functional genes—in addition to microbial composition.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::65d1d201a18946b88612ec88989dcf0cf75c17f3f27fd250b4782daff97ca912",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::cdee8c93e7f5408105b8b6e8c4d64ab28234e2f0bc1e3132ca74cd68f37e98d5",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::c13e54e776d7bd7066edd4d6": {
      "atom_id": "atom::c13e54e776d7bd7066edd4d6",
      "source_handle": "P0224",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "work_summary"
      ],
      "value": "This scoping review (Part II of a series) integrates findings from 83 studies (59 rodent, 24 human) that measured functional biomarkers alongside sleep/microbiome outcomes. It identifies consistent mechanistic links between sleep disruption and host homeostasis changes mediated by the microbiome, including HPA axis activation, altered bile acid metabolism, inflammation-related shifts, and disrupted tryptophan pathways. The authors argue that while taxonomic responses vary, functional signatures converge, suggesting metabolic and signaling biomarkers are more stable indicators of microbiome involvement in sleep pathology than composition alone.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::65d1d201a18946b88612ec88989dcf0cf75c17f3f27fd250b4782daff97ca912",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::e2fc8725756d4f2225ec5265eb6e734002786df8bc44d015b78c36ad43deed15",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::00deb1f9e6f26203343e7cef": {
      "atom_id": "atom::00deb1f9e6f26203343e7cef",
      "source_handle": "P0224",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "planning_summary"
      ],
      "value": "This paper provides a detailed mechanistic framework linking sleep/circadian disruption to gut microbiome function via neuroendocrine, immune, and metabolic pathways. While it does not directly address Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs), it offers critical background on how sleep dysregulation alters the gut environment (inflammation, barrier integrity, metabolite profiles) which may indirectly influence systemic immunity and potentially tumor microenvironment interactions relevant to solid tumors.",
      "role": "planner_interpretation",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::65d1d201a18946b88612ec88989dcf0cf75c17f3f27fd250b4782daff97ca912",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::2d6dd923ea1945553fca47d370f44b89c16602359aa519580e819aac27776126",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::fea750ba2244ba1eb85473d7": {
      "atom_id": "atom::fea750ba2244ba1eb85473d7",
      "source_handle": "P0224",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "Does not mention cancer or ICIs. The link to ICI efficacy is inferential based on general immunomodulatory effects.",
        "contribution": "Describes how sleep/circadian disruption creates a pro-inflammatory gut environment (increased LPS, cytokines, reduced SCFAs) and alters barrier integrity. This context is relevant for understanding baseline immune status which could modulate ICI efficacy.",
        "facet_id": "F1"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::65d1d201a18946b88612ec88989dcf0cf75c17f3f27fd250b4782daff97ca912",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::b59e688cb7638400d9eac323f981169fe5f26e6c65b422b910e60fc3ab3c5be5",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::5c08e4ab793bbab1a6f33bfb": {
      "atom_id": "atom::5c08e4ab793bbab1a6f33bfb",
      "source_handle": "P0224",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "Use to discuss how lifestyle factors like sleep deprivation might create a systemic inflammatory milieu that could theoretically antagonize anti-tumor immunity or alter the tumor microenvironment.",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::65d1d201a18946b88612ec88989dcf0cf75c17f3f27fd250b4782daff97ca912",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ad0541deda768fe690b632553e084d58c792528f59e28901e43b5f106d061f0b",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::5c89feeaed16541d08c41cd7": {
      "atom_id": "atom::5c89feeaed16541d08c41cd7",
      "source_handle": "P0224",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "Mechanisms described are in the context of sleep pathology, not cancer immunotherapy. Direct applicability to ICI resistance/sensitivity is not established.",
        "contribution": "Details specific mechanisms: HPA axis hyperactivity, TLR4/LPS signaling, FXR/TGR5 bile acid receptor signaling, and AhR activation by indoles. These are potential molecular targets or mediators of host-microbe-immune interactions.",
        "facet_id": "F2"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::65d1d201a18946b88612ec88989dcf0cf75c17f3f27fd250b4782daff97ca912",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
